# LAWS_conform.bend: every match the matcher answers conforms to its
# schema.
#
# The matcher (Sc.a1.s.m) works on A1Work items and answers a list of
# matches for each; cf.r says what each answer must be: nothing for
# A1WNone, one match per slot conforming to the slot's schema for
# A1WSlots, one match conforming to the schema for A1WOne. cf.m shows, by
# induction on the matcher's fuel f, that every Done answer is so at
# conformance fuel 2 f (a Fail needs nothing): each case of the matcher
# builds its answer from the answers to smaller work, through one helper
# per way of building (cf.cons and cf.slot_res for slots, cf.seq, cf.of,
# cf.choice, cf.expl and cf.opt for the schema forms). A sequence's slots
# carry its fields in order (cf.al), a SEQUENCE OF's slots all carry the
# item (cf.ofs), the alternative a CHOICE picks is one of its alternatives
# (cf.chx), and more fuel never hurts (cf.mono).
